From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Faizal <sahil.faizal@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] gdb: Keep finalization complaint flag access on main thread

The index cache writer calls cooked_index::wait from a worker after the
FINALIZED state has been published. The main thread can concurrently wait
for that same state and emit cached finalization complaints. Testing the
non-atomic m_finalize_complaints_emitted flag before is_main_thread reads
main-thread state from that worker, racing with the main-thread write.
The worker state mutex is released before either access to this flag.

Check thread identity first, so both the read and write remain confined
to the main thread, as intended by the existing comment and the matching
guard in cooked_index_worker::wait. Preserve complaint emission, worker
state synchronization and index-cache writing.

Reported by ConcurrencySanitizer after the functional CPU suite passed:
https://github.com/ROCm/TheRock/actions/runs/43021531939
Source: ROCm/rocgdb b79d66da2acad573ed4536d0ad1f042c48a98c69
Carry temporarily in TheRock pending upstream debugger review.
---
 gdb/dwarf2/cooked-index.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gdb/dwarf2/cooked-index.c b/gdb/dwarf2/cooked-index.c
index 2242ec8..79fcdb9 100644
--- a/gdb/dwarf2/cooked-index.c
+++ b/gdb/dwarf2/cooked-index.c
@@ -65,8 +65,8 @@ cooked_index::wait (cooked_state desired_state, bool allow_quit)
      here, we might have only asked for MAIN_AVAILABLE, but if the
      workers are quick then they might be done, in which case we
      should emit the complaints now.  */
-  if (!m_finalize_complaints_emitted
-      && is_main_thread ()
+  if (is_main_thread ()
+      && !m_finalize_complaints_emitted
       && (desired_state >= cooked_state::FINALIZED || done))
     {
       m_finalize_complaints_emitted = true;
-- 
